    overview_html: `<p>Sdorica operates a gacha system using Stones premium currency at $0.99 per single pull. The game features rotating limited-time character banners with 5-star drop rates typically 2% base and 5% featured rates. A hard 100-pull pity guarantees a featured 5-star character, with most acquisitions occurring before threshold. Rayark Games discloses rates clearly through in-game UI showing exact probabilities per rarity tier and featured character odds.</p><p>Free Stone income provides approximately 400-500 monthly currency, among the most generous in the industry. This supports 4-5 free pulls monthly, or one guaranteed pity every 2 months through pure free play. The monetization model emphasizes optional cosmetics and convenience items rather than gacha mechanics as primary revenue.</p><p>Sdorica features engaging narrative-driven gameplay with illustrated storybook aesthetic and tactical squad battles. The game's premium narrative quality and regular story updates create engagement depth beyond pure collection mentality.</p>`,
    pity_explanation_html: `<p>Sdorica implements an exceptionally player-friendly 100-pull hard pity system guaranteeing a featured 5-star character after 100 pulls without acquisition. Soft pity mechanisms increase featured rate-ups starting around pull 50-60, allowing most players to acquire targets well before hard pity. The dual-pity design combined with exceptional free Stone income makes acquisition highly accessible without spending.</p><p>The pity applies independently to each limited-time banner, resetting when featured characters change. However, the generous free Stone income allows sequential banner participation for free-to-play players without enforced multi-month saving periods between rolls.</p>`,
    history_html: `<p><strong>2017 Launch:</strong> Sdorica launched with innovative storybook aesthetic and generous monetization. Rayark Games emphasized player-friendly design and narrative quality from launch.</p><p><strong>2017-2025 Consistency:</strong> Sdorica has maintained exceptional monetization standards and free currency income for over 7 years. No aggressive monetization shifts occurred, with Rayark actively increasing free currency rewards through new events and activities.</p><p><strong>2020-2025 Story Expansion:</strong> Rayark focused on narrative quality improvements and expanding storybook content. The game prioritizes storytelling and character development alongside gacha mechanics.</p><p><strong>2025 Status:</strong> Sdorica continues thriving with exceptional player satisfaction scores. The game demonstrates that generous monetization creates sustainable long-term success and community loyalty.</p>`,
    controversy_html: `<p>Sdorica experiences minimal monetization-related controversy, with community discussions focused on story direction and character balance. Rayark's consistent player-friendly monetization generates broad trust in company values.</p><p>Some criticism exists regarding occasional limited-time exclusive characters, though Rayark typically re-runs these characters allowing eventual free acquisition through re-run banners.</p>`,
    tips_html: `<p><strong>1. Plan pity around story characters:</strong> The 400-500 monthly free Stones allow regular pity participation. Plan which story-significant characters interest you and commit free Stones to their banners.</p><p><strong>2. Engage with narrative content:</strong> Sdorica's primary value is storytelling quality. Read dialogue, engage with storybook progression, and experience narrative before focusing on gacha acquisition.</p><p><strong>3. Build teams around synergy rather than rarity:</strong> Tactical squad battles reward team composition and ability synergy. Many free and older characters remain viable through proper team building.</p><p><strong>4. Participate in all story events:</strong> Limited-time story events provide substantial Stone rewards and exclusive character acquisition opportunities. Active participation maximizes free currency income.</p><p><strong>5. Use cosmetics strategically:</strong> Optional cosmetics provide purely aesthetic changes. Prioritize gacha character acquisition over cosmetics when budgeting limited resources.</p>`,
    editorial_html: `<p>Sdorica exemplifies how consistent commitment to fair monetization creates exceptional long-term success and player loyalty. Rayark's 7+ year commitment to player-friendly design, generous free currency, and narrative quality demonstrates that aggressive extraction is choice, not necessity. The game thrives financially while respecting player boundaries.</p><p>The storybook aesthetic and narrative-driven gameplay separate Sdorica meaningfully from competitors. Rather than pure collection mechanics, the game emphasizes emotional story engagement and character development. This design philosophy attracts players seeking meaningful narrative experiences.</p><p>Rayark's willingness to re-run limited-time characters and provide multiple acquisition paths shows genuine player-friendliness beyond tokenistic pity systems. The company actively removes artificial scarcity through character re-runs, respecting late-joining player accessibility.</p><p>Rating: Highly recommended as exemplary gacha design. Sdorica represents the gold standard for fair monetization, generous free currency, and narrative quality. Both free-to-play and spending players find genuine value without exploitation. New players should start here as a benchmark for what fair gacha design achieves.</p>`
