    history_html: `<p><strong>2023 Launch:</strong> Whiteout Survival launched with survival-themed gameplay and aggressive monetization. The 50-pull pity threshold was significantly lower than competitors, suggesting monetization-first design.</p><p><strong>2023-2024 Growth:</strong> The game accumulated significant audience through gameplay engagement and seasonal competitive events. The lower pity threshold created frequent guaranteed acquisitions supporting spending motivation.</p><p><strong>2024-2025 Stability:</strong> Whiteout Survival maintains monetization structure with regular content updates. The game generates substantial revenue through competitive leaderboard spending pressure.</p>`,
    controversy_html: `<p>Whiteout Survival faces criticism for creating extreme seasonal competitive pressure where spending directly determines ranking success. Players feel forced into consistent monthly spending ($20-50+) to remain competitive in seasonal events. The limited free Gold income compounds this pressure, making pity participation difficult without spending.</p><p>Additionally, the lower 50-pull pity (while theoretically more generous) actually enables higher spending frequency, potentially encouraging budget-unconscious players to spend more regularly through perceived "easier" pity achievement.</p>`,
